# Constraint Change Benchmark Testing

When you modify a constraint implementation, you MUST run the constraint-family benchmark test
to verify no regressions. Use the class-to-family mapping below to determine the right filter.

## Command

```
mvn -pl jacop-benchmarks -am -Dtest=MinizincByConstraintTest -DconstraintFilter=<FAMILY> -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test
```

Add `-DtimeFilter=upTo5sec` for a fast check, or omit it to use the default (upTo30sec).

## Class-to-Family Mapping

| Constraint classes modified | `-DconstraintFilter` value |
|-----------------------------|---------------------------|
| `Alldiff`, `Alldifferent`, `Alldistinct`, `AlldifferentExcept*`, `SoftAlldifferent`, `AllEqual` | `alldifferent` |
| `GCC`, `SoftGCC` | `gcc` |
| `Cumulative*`, `CumulativeBasic`, `CumulativeUnary*` | `cumulative` |
| `Circuit`, `Subcircuit` | `circuit` |
| `ElementInteger*`, `ElementVariable*` | `element` |
| `Table`, `SimpleTable`, `TableMill` | `table` |
| `Regular`, `RegState*`, `RegEdge` | `regular` |
| `Knapsack` | `knapsack` |
| `Binpacking` | `binpacking` |
| `Diffn`, `Diff`, `Diff2*`, `DisjointConditional*` | `diffn` |
| `LinearInt*`, `SumInt`, `SumBool`, `Sum`, `SumWeight` | `linear` |
| `Xeq*`, `Xneq*`, `Xlt*`, `Xlteq*`, `Xgt*` | `comparison` |
| `And`, `Or`, `Not`, `Xor`, `BoolClause`, `*BoolVector` | `boolean` |
| `AbsXeqY`, `Distance`, `XmulY*`, `XdivY*`, `XmodY*`, `XexpY*`, `XplusY*` | `arithmetic` |
| `Count*`, `Among*`, `Values`, `AtLeast`, `AtMost` | `counting` |
| `LexOrder`, `Lex`, `Increasing`, `Decreasing`, `SeqPrecedeChain` | `ordering` |
| `NetworkFlow`, `NetworkBuilder` | `networkflow` |
| `Geost`, `GeostObject`, `Shape` | `geost` |
| `Sequence`, `Stretch`, `ValuePrecede` | `sequence` |
| `Assignment` | `assignment` |
| `Min`, `Max`, `ArgMin`, `ArgMax` | `minmax` |
| `Member` | `member` |
| Set constraints (`set/constraints/`) | `set` |
| Float constraints (`floats/constraints/`) | `float` |
| Graph constraints | `graph` |

When multiple families are affected, combine them: `-DconstraintFilter=cumulative,diffn`.
